      "category": "rust_runtime_check",
      "rust_error": null,
      "claim": "Fixed-width u64 arithmetic compiled with overflow checks panics on the overflowing deposit natively, and the project compiler emits checked arithmetic that rejects it in CLVM; Chialisp integers grow without bound.",
      "limitations": [
        "Native overflow behavior depends on compiler settings; this study enables overflow checks explicitly, and the corrected fixture uses checked_add so the rejection no longer depends on them.",
        "The compiled-subset credit is the referenced corpus case, where the independent Chialisp module accepts the unbounded sum and the Rust CLVM rejects it in both optimizer modes; that is finite executed evidence, not a compiler-preservation proof.",
        "Rue Int is unbounded by design, so the Rue translation reproduces the growth; a bounded Rue type or explicit guard would be needed."
      ],
      "caught_by": [
        "native_rust_overflow_check",
        "compiled_checked_arithmetic"
      ],
